#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c089ac0-6345-5a8c-b62f-0ed057920e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c089ac0-6345-5a8c-b62f-0ed057920e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293300} :answer-field/id #uuid "07bd3ca9-b08b-5bba-b233-e5435a9a2640" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "593dad82-9cf7-57f0-a8f9-1d4350843ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "593dad82-9cf7-57f0-a8f9-1d4350843ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293290} :answer-field/id #uuid "2929fa13-2cfd-51a7-8f49-b45196662e2c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e10f888-66d4-5375-8f79-b8da98cf5664" :question/math-academy-id "q-282261" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,0,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,2,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{29}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ x & 0 & 1 \\\\ -x & 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 2\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0-2)i-(0+x)j+(2x+0)k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-x,2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4} & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4 & =29 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},$ $x=\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fe042d9-f712-540a-9a31-4c3f6a49c2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe042d9-f712-540a-9a31-4c3f6a49c2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293064} :answer-field/id #uuid "472a2680-c3e4-5a4b-bf63-8a3b7676904d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8df1edb2-60a1-5e25-a033-c22d6600a279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8df1edb2-60a1-5e25-a033-c22d6600a279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293481} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc407dd-1a3f-56e7-be3e-e7615f20ae61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "999eb6f6-f5c6-519d-9ac7-4875fbf986b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-282262" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d647f4-bc4e-5f76-acc3-d8205ef31c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40d647f4-bc4e-5f76-acc3-d8205ef31c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293195} :answer-field/id #uuid "8623129c-f6e8-53ae-bd31-d59d37637d0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59e9fba3-4db6-5c48-86ed-2af0a557b731" :question/math-academy-id "q-282269" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{10}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(3x-1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨3,1-3x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(1-3x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11} & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-6x+11 & =10 \\\\ (3x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63fe025d-813b-5f9a-9c06-c0556ddb9547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63fe025d-813b-5f9a-9c06-c0556ddb9547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293343} :answer-field/id #uuid "c20c34ca-4ea2-51bf-9889-6f3124593e13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7de1193-053f-5234-9520-07973769fe4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-282270" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cb1d18-d1e0-565d-bb78-b6a4658bbe13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09cb1d18-d1e0-565d-bb78-b6a4658bbe13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292974} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c55d87-7acb-572f-811d-7189f6ef9993" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b32daaa-10cc-5583-9726-450366961c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b32daaa-10cc-5583-9726-450366961c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292978} :answer-field/id #uuid "508dcba7-f96e-5b1d-99d9-43b1a4ce626c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe9d7249-168a-5810-85b9-89bad6dafc21" :question/math-academy-id "q-282276" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,4,5⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{33}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ x & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}x & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(4-0)i-(x-5)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨4,5-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(5-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+(25-10x+{x}^{2})+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+57} & =\\sqrt{33} \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+57 & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x+24 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =4,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=4,$ $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a3a765-13c2-5f3d-89c8-752a0cc1e107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44a3a765-13c2-5f3d-89c8-752a0cc1e107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293214} :answer-field/id #uuid "c018ffe1-59c2-5c29-85ed-cac2b8dc9161" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6e2225-14bc-5817-b2b0-9fa7c511b22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e6e2225-14bc-5817-b2b0-9fa7c511b22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293441} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a690fb-f7f4-52fd-8017-428f88655eec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9b76997-cb19-548e-a5c8-ac57874f667e" :question/math-academy-id "q-282278" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "144a6036-1a43-5c55-bd4d-8c3b921ab81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-\\sqrt{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295382} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4bc189-56e8-506b-afae-8c32583fd169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4+\\sqrt{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295423} {:answer/id #uuid "4809f8aa-d435-582b-a813-64757ceea05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295678} {:answer/id #uuid "598e8e48-0407-5a12-b4c7-8a90c76b22d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295784} {:answer/id #uuid "addb0989-293c-52f5-817b-1eac8428806e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4+\\sqrt{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "144a6036-1a43-5c55-bd4d-8c3b921ab81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-\\sqrt{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295382} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0a2dd69-37ef-5e8e-92ea-d1b66a49d028" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "380886ef-0fbf-54bc-9579-e4e21dd4f7ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-29673" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/2+1}}{-\\frac{5}{2}+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-3/2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{3}}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{2})^{3}}-\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{1})^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-4}{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4-\\sqrt{2}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bd7f17-ab32-5370-92e4-2c424857d4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\sqrt{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295668} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa0b422-cd22-5a1d-9b1e-fc3b0fec4206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\sqrt[3]{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296113} {:answer/id #uuid "a8df53ed-dfab-5400-9e39-0f11c871eb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\sqrt[3]{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296156} {:answer/id #uuid "cef9375b-09ce-5562-9390-f6e2d91c89a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296354} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0dc99e-e1e1-515f-bf48-ed2f135dba0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\sqrt[3]{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff0dc99e-e1e1-515f-bf48-ed2f135dba0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\sqrt[3]{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296626} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8b2292-328d-5882-8739-6f5ed9a71d13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2d4f351a-f228-5a07-9853-4d4d86412f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-29674" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{-4/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4/3+1}}{-\\frac{4}{3}+1}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-3{x}^{-1/3}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{1}}) \\\\  & =3(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}) \\\\  & =3-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{3}} \\\\  & =3-\\sqrt[3]{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a3c276e-b651-5a89-8bbb-3d7a97126676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295422} {:answer/id #uuid "327ac714-bc95-59b2-b101-f216e5da9dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{31}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295552} {:answer/id #uuid "be25b993-b7fc-5022-8518-637847503cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296270} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc6bef6-c4a7-50b7-9e5b-b2fb380271e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296430} {:answer/id #uuid "eb296243-699c-57d5-9c9f-c7d5850cd2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be25b993-b7fc-5022-8518-637847503cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296270} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e0ad488-8a1c-5ff2-88cc-a11b58276dea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85c7a44a-100b-573e-a54f-0ac01a135d81" :question/math-academy-id "q-29746" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{4+1}}{4+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{5}}{5}-\\frac{{1}^{5}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c985339-e8a9-5013-a7bc-4e49a05cf16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295337} {:answer/id #uuid "34818e95-d9d8-5f6e-89ad-2ac8fabf3e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295561} {:answer/id #uuid "d1461848-8a61-5745-9f24-b274a9ed68fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296367} {:answer/id #uuid "e5952e24-a6e0-5920-9fa8-3940a0d816f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296490} {:answer/id #uuid "edfd70da-f5e3-54ac-806b-e2aafc609d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34818e95-d9d8-5f6e-89ad-2ac8fabf3e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295561} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c7215c-4387-5294-8949-1c572219b286" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "078e36f8-ac04-5dc6-872a-8aad0a6d9513" :question/math-academy-id "q-29747" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{-4+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3}}{(-3)}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{8}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb26afef-455b-5297-b622-9e232fa102cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296332} {:answer/id #uuid "80839a19-547c-4ca2-94bb-993fa3f9a75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577458} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcd2965-c659-42b4-96df-25a652585597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\left(2x\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577459} {:answer/id #uuid "886e5238-5128-4041-b4c9-6957e06baf70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\left(2x+7\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577460} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0bf0d4-06da-4ccd-9691-c576056d141e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\left(2x+7\\right)^{-}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577461} {:answer/id #uuid "cab10951-ff4e-46a1-9533-9c912f129e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\left(2x+7\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{\\placeholder{}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577462} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe2d8e8-70df-4e73-95b1-9c1880cd800a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\left(2x+7\\right)^{-\\frac32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb26afef-455b-5297-b622-9e232fa102cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296332} :answer-field/id #uuid "69dfefe3-2eb8-5512-ab7d-eb2788925109" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2300bd8f-e3d1-544c-8ad1-127cb2f0bedc" :question/math-academy-id "q-314194" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+7}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x+7.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7{)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297435 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b4bd4d3-ecef-583b-97fc-f8705c9edda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b4bd4d3-ecef-583b-97fc-f8705c9edda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295327} :answer-field/id #uuid "64c5f7bf-a4b8-5df1-8864-2006341a5555" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "719a311f-6c8f-513c-84dc-85675a6f24ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-315984" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{80}{4} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815b59ac-66aa-50b6-8f74-d5f9c6d253c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "815b59ac-66aa-50b6-8f74-d5f9c6d253c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295962} :answer-field/id #uuid "619e4438-91be-5a7e-9594-a0155f226327" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41aa5101-c6e0-5e2e-af55-4009a409fb57" :question/math-academy-id "q-315985" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{-2}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{2\\cdot {3}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot {1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{18}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299580 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a5bc8d5-e509-5863-b1b0-5d966475a48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a5bc8d5-e509-5863-b1b0-5d966475a48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298152} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e520c21-8113-540a-a136-ed9d09b72c68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e756bda8-091e-58df-91a3-7d6c4fd6790c" :question/math-academy-id "q-317302" :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{7})+(-2)(3)+(5)(-1) \\\\  & =7-6-5 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299581 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "642b83ad-84f3-53a2-ae75-f108cc2a5be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "642b83ad-84f3-53a2-ae75-f108cc2a5be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297978} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf93de4a-48e1-5dad-a599-646066d80847" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dcaa5f3b-4be2-5705-929a-5ba642430c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-317303" :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-\\sqrt{8},\\,4,\\,-3⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{8},\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-\\sqrt{8},\\,4,\\,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{8},\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{8})(\\sqrt{8})+(4)(-1)+(-3)(2) \\\\  & =-8-4-6 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f46a08c3-ac51-5443-9d62-4a4fdbe6834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f46a08c3-ac51-5443-9d62-4a4fdbe6834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298591} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a67eb77-f73b-57a3-9ceb-4843468c5708" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47306bb8-b679-542e-9111-9cf80b931f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-317304" :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩\\cdot ⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩ \\\\  & =(0)(7)+(5)(-2)+(\\sqrt{11})(\\sqrt{11}) \\\\  & =0-10+11 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771cc149-2f2f-5147-82d6-b25bff5aa208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "771cc149-2f2f-5147-82d6-b25bff5aa208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298071} :answer-field/id #uuid "c69c83b4-8ce3-5770-b7b0-9b88367956e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7f80b43-a2f5-515b-92f2-1141b2bd6cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-317312" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,-1,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 1)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2\\,(19)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(8) \\\\  & =38+2+24 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c961519-b921-5775-827d-a9cadb1e6380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c961519-b921-5775-827d-a9cadb1e6380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297944} :answer-field/id #uuid "c381c136-ee2c-58cf-bde0-10864ff1fed7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4cbf30f6-1867-5976-9eac-2960f6231475" :question/math-academy-id "q-317315" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,-1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =1\\,(1)\\,-\\,2\\,(22)\\,+\\,3\\,(-4) \\\\  & =1-44-12 \\\\  & =-55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f144fd50-d589-55a7-a6ca-f89363fa3f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f144fd50-d589-55a7-a6ca-f89363fa3f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298572} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ab6799f-51df-5f98-b17e-12fedf7852db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2672a60f-3785-5ec9-9526-2daad7a5333b" :question/math-academy-id "q-317316" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,-1,-2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\,(1\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(3\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,5\\,(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =0(-2)\\,-\\,2\\,(-6)\\,+\\,5\\,(-7) \\\\  & =0+12-35 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cd6328a-133b-5e12-8514-1efaa6b6d672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cd6328a-133b-5e12-8514-1efaa6b6d672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298022} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ebcaea2-b965-5e9e-8bcc-7aeba6a2af03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e752a1da-5c2f-551a-a669-66eee02c7b08" :question/math-academy-id "q-317317" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨5,6,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 6)\\,-\\,2\\,(4\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 5)\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot 6-0\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =1\\,(12)\\,-\\,2\\,(14)\\,+\\,3\\,(24) \\\\  & =12-28+72 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eadf82fd-7365-5e8c-a894-8da47cecc210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eadf82fd-7365-5e8c-a894-8da47cecc210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298550} :answer-field/id #uuid "d53ab5af-4297-5b00-921b-5e024f7f4a79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffaceba3-4514-5d9f-9674-fd0da3b7e455" :question/math-academy-id "q-317319" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,1,3⟩$, $b=⟨1,4,0⟩$ and $c=⟨6,-1,2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,1\\,(1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 6)\\,+\\,3\\,(1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =2\\,(8)\\,-\\,1\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(-25) \\\\  & =16-2-75 \\\\  & =-61.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35fa7689-3f81-5526-9891-34fe7b851cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35fa7689-3f81-5526-9891-34fe7b851cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297768} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a80f5f4-0960-5b1b-b809-d436a1df0f7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8459484-168d-53bc-8fac-703a96f7dc80" :question/math-academy-id "q-317320" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,2,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,0\\,(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,2\\,(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =1\\,(5)\\,-\\,0\\,(15)\\,+\\,2\\,(2) \\\\  & =5+0+4 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299589 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb1dcb9-396f-5eaa-8775-f72db38b1cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fb1dcb9-396f-5eaa-8775-f72db38b1cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297754} :answer-field/id #uuid "51174c90-0c81-50cc-80c5-54b698c7ea80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1b3c364-d315-5da6-9fc0-ab4b2a4285e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-317322" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,1,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,4⟩$ and $c=⟨5,2,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\,(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,1\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 5)\\,+\\,0\\,(0\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =2\\,(-5)\\,-\\,1\\,(-20)\\,+\\,0\\,(-15) \\\\  & =-10+20+0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb9271c-ec63-545e-82bd-3098f3d6d52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbb9271c-ec63-545e-82bd-3098f3d6d52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298372} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba217f0a-f30a-560e-b9be-570832c81a18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86560436-5dd3-5177-80a9-3ddb91ccbf81" :question/math-academy-id "q-317325" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,-2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,-1,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\,-\\,(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\,+\\,3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\,((-1)(-3)-(-2)\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,(-2)\\,(4\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot 1)\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =(-1)\\,(7)\\,-\\,(-2)\\,(-10)\\,+\\,3\\,(9) \\\\  & =-7-20+27 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ce25fc2-f172-5796-bdb4-80f062501242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ce25fc2-f172-5796-bdb4-80f062501242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298240} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ec026c-9601-596a-aac7-34e1c7298d90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52b70b4e-c944-5a6c-9fb5-10e8bb1b8364" :question/math-academy-id "q-317335" :question/problem "Calculate $det(R)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle R=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(R)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(8)(4)-(-5)(3) \\\\  & =32+15 \\\\  & =47.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56075e41-2276-59fc-aa32-dc0aefbc46ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56075e41-2276-59fc-aa32-dc0aefbc46ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297914} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd2ce63-3870-5dc7-88b5-af30fb44581f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51e6ce71-0f6b-5ca6-9047-0832d38b3af3" :question/math-academy-id "q-317336" :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2)(3)-(4)(1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6324678-0597-5421-a104-04c3342494f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6324678-0597-5421-a104-04c3342494f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298419} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc4e21a-193b-52dd-8dc9-d21c2d8f7ddb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd3c7419-67b1-5120-a5e4-6bd19d8d0a71" :question/math-academy-id "q-317342" :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(6)(7)-(-2)(5) \\\\  & =42+10 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c76837d-abf1-5987-8d19-edc1988fecd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c76837d-abf1-5987-8d19-edc1988fecd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297738} :answer-field/id #uuid "f75cec09-3e63-55a8-bfe9-30a9430f9ad5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ef37e01-1bf6-55b3-89e8-cc90cafd078c" :question/math-academy-id "q-317343" :question/problem "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨4,-1,6⟩$ and $a=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$\n\n$b\\cdot (c\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-1,6⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =8-3-6 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4b2714-199b-59fe-a41f-f7e979f3f9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d4b2714-199b-59fe-a41f-f7e979f3f9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297616} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac069ea-97f0-5b28-aae8-5ec01ea01538" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6ca014c-b5cb-5825-95b8-87e00a3142c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-317367" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3706ac16-28a9-5ab4-9e33-623654c6773f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{37}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3706ac16-28a9-5ab4-9e33-623654c6773f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{37}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297774} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab4d4b7-2252-5c08-b2b6-6e240fa0a5f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a27ba74d-67e7-552a-808b-c86c1ab2858a" :question/math-academy-id "q-317368" :question/problem "Calculate $det(E)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(E)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(E) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{37}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
